First excavation batch is complete and appended to `WORKSPACES/COMMON/NATHAN_VERIFIED_WORDS_COMPENDIUM.md`.

I inspected the raw `Geometry in Physics` export directly—3,280 mapping nodes—and accepted passages only where the raw metadata explicitly gives `author.role = user`. Six verified Nathan messages were added, covering June 8–10, 2026:

- tracing the time-surface idea;
- electron as a single-coil worldline/tube, quark 2-/3-braids, and bosons as filament vibrations;
- geometry as a way of approaching physics you did not already understand;
- the early provenance of “timesheet” and “world line” vocabulary;
- the historical shift in θ₄ language from “filament-time energy transfer” to “timesheet drag”;
- the Minkowski worldline diagram and early dimensional-thinking provenance.

Each entry preserves exact wording, Eastern timestamp, raw message ID, durable repository path, tags, immediate context, and a deliberately separate status/correction field. I also added a coverage ledger so later runs know exactly what has and has not been scanned.

No uncertain-authorship text was promoted.

Current unresolved retrieval issues: I have not yet materialized the raw `DIMENSIONAL GRAVITY` export. I also located a `SAT Overview — raw.json` copy with explicit raw user metadata, but that particular Library copy does not permit raw-byte materialization.

Next excavation priority is `DIMENSIONAL GRAVITY`, followed by `SAT Overview`, `Reasoning with SAT-HSH Skill`, `H(s)H TIME RESIDUALS`, and the June–July worldline→worldtube conversations—especially direct corrections involving dimensionality, timesheet/intersection propagation, rest versus motion, and finite-thickness readout.

Fifth excavation batch is complete and appended to `WORKSPACES/COMMON/NATHAN_VERIFIED_WORDS_COMPENDIUM.md`.

This pass added **4 verified Nathan messages** from `DIMENSIONAL GRAVITY — raw.json`, covering late March 28, 2024 and the June 1, 2026 revisit:

- interaction history as an additional cross-spacetime ingredient in the early SAT picture;
- your question about whether greater future-directed tangling could produce an inward/past-directed energy-transfer bias;
- the historical proposal that high-energy events might affect matter connected to them through past or future interaction history;
- your 2026 qualification of the uploaded later formalization: “That’s our theory today. Well… one of the countless variations.”

That last one is especially useful provenance-wise because it prevents `SAT.4DHH.UC.pdf` from being treated as a uniquely canonical endpoint merely because it was shown to the older instance.

I excluded all of the large tool-injected `SAT.4DHH.UC.pdf` passages from the compendium. They appeared inside the raw conversation, but their metadata identifies them as tool/file-search content rather than Nathan-authored messages.

The durable update is commit `ef89028cca22564e03740bb96ac4591c1e9dce38`.

`DIMENSIONAL GRAVITY` is now substantially sampled across its original 2024 development and its 2026 revisit, though it has not been exhaustively read message-by-message. The next target is the durable raw `SAT Overview` conversation if I can resolve its exact GitHub path; otherwise I’ll move directly into `Reasoning with SAT-HSH Skill`, followed by `H(s)H TIME RESIDUALS`, with emphasis on your direct corrections about dimensionality, worldline/worldtube typing, timesheet/intersection propagation, and source/model status.

Sixth excavation batch is complete and appended to `WORKSPACES/COMMON/NATHAN_VERIFIED_WORDS_COMPENDIUM.md`.

This pass moved into the durable raw `SAT Overview` conversation and added **5 verified Nathan messages from June 23, 2026**, each backed by raw `author.role = user` metadata:

- your hedged overview of timesheet-drag/GR, braid morphology/QCD, and the incompleteness of the roundup documents;
- the especially useful “one structure” description: a recursively nested **helical worldline/worldtube**, with the scaling architecture explicitly left unresolved;
- your explicit classification of **UI/TX and Donut/Whirlygig as tools**;
- the provenance statement that **`FINDING THE DONUT` is your original formulation**, with the other attached Donut documents being attempts to make it work;
- your distinction between what you regard as geometrically evident and the separate future task of establishing the Donut’s formal capabilities.

I deliberately did **not** promote a high-value passage about worldlines being an essentialized representation relative to worldtubes, including radius/pitch scaling, because although its wording was recovered from the indexed raw corpus, I did not recover an explicit raw user-role node for that exact message in this pass.

The durable update is commit `1e6bfa67773b4555e89114f328ca1b94a4d52224`.

Next excavation region is later June 23 through July 5 in `SAT Overview`, concentrating on worldtube/finite-core typing, radius/pitch/arclength, UI/Donut/Whirligig, Spheres/Graticule, and direct model-status corrections. After that: `Reasoning with SAT-HSH Skill` and `H(s)H TIME RESIDUALS`.

